# quaff, recite, brandish and zap: obj_cast_spell's checks, and then the spell. In the temple (3001): Pickpocket (13,
# scrolls, staves and wands at 75%: an 80% chance) and Decimus (10, in no clan). Each object is made and picked up just
# before it's used, mostly with its values set: pink potions (105) with no spell and with sword (a skill, so "That's not
# a spell!"), a potion of divine protection (3082, level 16: too high), old scrolls (1362) with no spell, a scroll of
# recall (3042, level 17), burnt staves (1327) with no charges, with identify (a target brandish can't use), with spell
# 140 (a row of skill_table past its end, all zeros) and with sword, small wands (106) with no charges, with sword and
# with kick (an offensive skill, so Decimus, in no clan, is safe from it, and a box has no victim: zapped or recited
# at), a box (3033), and a pink potion of identify, which needs an object. A staff or wand above its holder's level
# can't be held (wear_obj), so brandish's and zap's own level checks never fail. Last, a pink potion casts invisibility
# (a spell for a character or an object) on whoever quaffs it.
@connect pick
Pickpocket
psswrd
@return
@connect dec
Decimus
psswrd
@return
@return
@as pick
@obj 3033 3001
get box
quaff
quaff nothing
quaff box
@obj 3082 3001
get divine
quaff divine
@obj 105 3001 6 -1 -1 -1 -1
get pink
quaff pink
@obj 105 3001 6 105 -1 -1 -1
get pink
quaff pink
recite
recite box
@obj 3042 3001
get recall
recite recall
@obj 1362 3001 10 -1 -1 -1 -1
@obj 1362 3001 10 -1 -1 -1 -1
@obj 1362 3001 10 -1 -1 -1 -1
@obj 1362 3001 10 -1 -1 -1 -1
get all.old
recite old nobody
recite old decimus
recite old box
recite old
recite old
brandish
zap
zap decimus
